{"name":"Scoville Highness","hex":"#900405","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being high.","A title of respect when referring to a prince or princess."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scoville scale","blocks":[{"text":"The Scoville scale is a measurement of spiciness of chili peppers and other substances, recorded in Scoville heat units (SHU). It is based on the concentration of capsaicinoids, among which capsaicin is the predominant component."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG/330px-PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scoville_scale"},{"title":"Highness","blocks":[{"text":"Highness is a formal style used to address or refer to certain members of a reigning or formerly reigning dynasty. It is typically used with a possessive adjective: \"His Highness\", \"Her Highness\" (HH), \"Their Highnesses\" (TH), etc. Although often combined with other adjectives of honour indicating rank, such as \"Imperial\", \"Royal\" or \"Serene\", it may be used alone."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg/500px-BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg/1280px-BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg/500px-BhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The ghost pepper of Northeast India is considered to be a \"very hot\" pepper, at about 1 million SHU.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABhutJolokia09_Asit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg/500px-Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg/1280px-Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg/500px-Naga_jolokia_chili.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Naga Morich, with around 1 million SHU,[2] is primarily grown in Bangladesh and India.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANaga_jolokia_chili.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Red_savina_cropped.jpg/500px-Red_savina_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Red_savina_cropped.jpg/500px-Red_savina_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Red Savina pepper, a hot chili[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_savina_cropped.jpg"}],"sounds":{"highness":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/En-us-highness.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/97/En-us-highness.ogg/En-us-highness.ogg.mp3"}]}}}